-- title:
--   Normalised Hahn-series embeddings induce places of F_N
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number and let $j_0$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (realised as `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`). Write $\overline{F_N}$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image, under the coefficient-extension embedding `coeffEmb`, of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the family `divisorExpansions N`. Let $\psi$ be an element of `Emb N j₀`, that is, a pair consisting of an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra homomorphism $\psi_1$ from $\overline{F_N}$ into the field `HahnSeries ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` of Hahn series with rational exponents and coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, together with the normalisation that $\psi_1$ sends `jBar N` (the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$) to $j_0 + q$, i.e. to the constant series $j_0$ plus the monomial of exponent $1$ and coefficient $1$. The assertion is that there exist a place $w$ of $\overline{F_N}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a valuation subring of $\overline{F_N}$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring — and a rational number $g > 0$ such that for every $x \in \overline{F_N}$ one has $(\operatorname{ord}_w x)\, g = \operatorname{order}(\psi_1 x)$, where $\operatorname{ord}_w x$ is the integer $-\log$ of the adic valuation of $x$ at $w$ and $\operatorname{order}$ is the exponent of the leading term of a Hahn series.
--
--   This is the step that converts a normalised Hahn-series expansion of the level $N$ modular function field at $j_0$ into a genuine place of that field, with the orders of vanishing matching up to a single positive rational factor (the reciprocal of the ramification index over $j_0$). It is used in the counting of places where `jBar` has order one, in [`ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_eq_one_eq_nuThree`](thm.html#ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_eq_one_eq_nuThree) and [`ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_sub_1728_eq_one_eq_nuTwo`](thm.html#ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_sub_1728_eq_one_eq_nuTwo), and in [`ModularCurve.emd_holds`](thm.html#ModularCurve.emd_holds).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_place_of_emb.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_EMD
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_MazurStepThreeInputs
import Definitions.Def_HahnSeries_RamificationBound
